Z||000000||Monkeyman||12-19-1999||03:27 AM||||Does anyone know if the grille inside the notchback taillights comes out?  I'd like to remove it, but I can't find any reference to that in my Haynes manual and I'd hate to spend the time (outside in the snow) to remove the assy if I can't get the grille out.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||12-19-1999||04:59 AM||||From what I remember, they're an integral part of the taillight assy.  They do come out, but you can't put the light's back together w/o 'em.  I don't like 'em either, so I took a look see one day...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||12-19-1999||06:40 AM||||What do you mean I "can't put the lights back together without them"?  Will the lens fit too loosely?  Or will the lamp assy be loose?  I'm trying to figure out a way to put a design on the taillight lenses.  (There was a thread about this.)  I have some ideas, but I need to have the grille removed from in front of (?behind?) the lights to do this.  If the grille is in place, it will show through and it won't work?  Maybe I'll take the lens off and see what I can figure out.  <P>OK.  Now I can't find my Haynes manual!  How do you get the lenses off?<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 12-19-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||12-19-1999||10:54 AM||||Just pop the black plastic screw hole covers, undo the screwst to take out the tail lights. Look and it will be very plain how they come apart and yes the red plastic comes right out so you can paint the clear lens with any design you like.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||12-19-1999||10:56 AM||||After you open the trunk, you'll see 6 square black plastic covers across the back above the taillights. Carefully pop these off and unscrew the long taillight holder screw thingies out. Twist off the bulb assemblies and you can remove the whole lens unit. Plastic clips (and a little black gooey sealer) hold the clear lens on. The rest of the taillight assemble is one unit I think. The back side of the outer clear lens is where we were talking about putting a design.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||12-19-1999||12:45 PM||||Backside meaning inside, right?  Would it get too hot to put vinyl in there?  I'm talking about the kind used for graphics on cars, etc.  My brain's been working overtime on this.||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||12-19-1999||02:01 PM||||It ought to be ok, just don't try using those bright halogen taillight bulbs, those will bake plastic.||||reg||1
