Z||000010||Phil||12-19-1999||09:39 PM||||I went to my local auto paint supply store and got a box of 3M strip caulk (part # 08578) 20yds. about $6. They are strips(duh) of a black clay like stuff to use as flexable weather caulking. I used it as an adhesive to replace the vapor barrier on my door panels, looks as if it would be just the thing to reseal the lights.||||reg||1
Z||000011||DXR_DAD||12-19-1999||09:43 PM||||Monkeyman I was going to just make the back up light another tail light/Brake light?? I think the thing with the seal is that you get it into the grove good and around the clips that hold the two together and use a good silicone or form-a-gasket? Check the bone yard for white/clear lenes that will fit the bumper opening, this shouldn't be that hard to find. The whole mod should not even cost that much and I think It will add a little style to the tail light set up. Iam going to start on this mod also. let me know what you come up with.||||reg||14
