Z||000013||Monkeyman||12-20-1999||01:51 PM||||The only price I've seen was something like $50US for the control.  That didn't seem too outrageous, but I may have misread something.  The problem isn't that you're logging on late (I do that all the time).  The problem is the quantity/quality of your medication. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Tell your doctor that the dementia is returning and you need him to up your dosage.  (It worked for me. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>I have some old bicycle turn signal lights (anybody remember when you could get a little generator for a bike?) in the garage that will fit perfectly in the rear bumper.  There is a mounting bolt coming through the bottom that will have to be relocated, but I think it will work.  I looked in a catalog for a truck stop chrome shop and they have clear lenses that will fit this.  If the freezing rain and wind ever stop, I'll go outside and remove my taillight lens and try to get started.  (We now have an inch of ice on the ground and I don't think I can get to my car without falling on my a**!)||||reg||1
Z||000014||Monkeyman||12-20-1999||02:51 PM||||I just got tail light lens off of the car.  (Plastic sure is brittle when it's cold! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">)  I got everything apart and, when I either get a heater for the garage or it gets warmer, I'll go to work on this.  BTW-I don't think I need the grilles anymore.  The bulbs are standard 1156s and I think I can get red rubber covers for those.  I'll have to check my sources.  <P>Here's another question.  (I don't have anyone at the moment who can help me with this)  There are 3 bulbs in the red section.  Which operate for the turn signal and which operate for the brakes?  Would it be possible to run wires from one of the other lamps to the lamp that goes to the reverse light?  I can take those wires and run them to my new reverse lite in the bumper.  Someone let me know soon as I'm itching to get started on this.  (Maybe the itching is due to dandruff, I don't know)||||reg||1
Z||000015||DRH||12-20-1999||03:44 PM||||This is all assuming you don't have a fastback. They are different. <BR>For all others: The turn signal and brake are the same circuit. The turn signal switch determines whether it gets constant on for brakes or on/off for turn. The 2 outside bulbs are tail light and brake/turn. The inner bulb is tail light only. The outer bulbs should have 3 wires (tail, brake/turn and ground). The inner red bulb should have 2 wires (tail and ground). The backup light should have 2 wires (backup and ground). You should be able to rewire them any way you like. The catch would be if you want the inner red bulb or the backup light bulb to be both tail light and turn/brake light you will need 3 wire sockets (junkyard?) and the right type bulbs (same as outer). Also, if you increase the number of turn signal bulbs you may need to change the flasher to get the right "blink" rate. Which wire does what shouldn't be too hard to figure out. I can check the wire colors if you need me to though.<BR>There was a thread a while back with a link to a place that sold the sequential kit for $50 or $60. I think it required replacing the inner bulb socket to get all 3 red lights to flash sequntially. Not sure if it could be made to flash the former backup light also.||||reg||1
